  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "As Wikipedia records, The New York Times reported on November 11, 2026, that Huang had a second affair with Nvidia's vice president of healthcare, Kimberly Powell, a married woman who reports to him.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385563690:84"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:12Z",
      "text": "Jen-Hsun \"Jensen\" Huang, born February 17, 1963, is a Taiwanese and American electrical engineer and businessman.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385563690:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Huang was born in Taipei on 17 February 1963.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P569",
        "wd:Q305177:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "He was educated at Stanford University, Aloha High School and Oneida Baptist Institute, among 2 more schools.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q41506",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q4734192",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q7093656",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q7375693",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q861888"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "Records also show that he worked in Los Altos.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P937:Q864124"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "On record are 6 awards, including the Queen Elizabeth Prize for Engineering in 2025 and the National Medal of Science in 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P166:Q4273323",
        "wd:Q305177:P166:Q737051"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:00:57Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to the Nvidia article, which drew 123,851 readers, and the Lisa Su article, which drew 62,648.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Nvidia:2026-11-10",
        "views:en:Lisa_Su:2026-11-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:01:06Z",
      "text": "On 10 November 2026, 542,553 people read the English article, about 73 times the usual level.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Jensen_Huang:2026-11-10",
        "views:en:Jensen_Huang:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:01:13Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 10 languages, and after English, the largest readership was in Chinese, with 65,740 readers.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Jensen_Huang:2026-11-10",
        "views:zh:黃仁勳:2026-11-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:01:20Z",
      "text": "Each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, though a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:zh:黃仁勳:2026-11-10",
        "views:ja:ジェンスン・フアン:2026-11-10",
        "views:es:Jensen_Huang:2026-11-10",
        "views:fr:Jensen_Huang:2026-11-10",
        "views:pt:Jensen_Huang:2026-11-10",
        "views:ru:Хуанг,_Дженсен:2026-11-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-10T00:01:30Z",
      "text": "The sources are Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata, and each caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385563690:84",
        "views:en:Jensen_Huang:2026-11-10",
